---
title: Yay Management
order: 2
description: yay -Yc, --cleanafter, --diff, --editmenu
tags: [yay, clean, config, diff, management]
---

Managing yay configuration, build artifacts, and review workflows.

@code bash
# ---- cleanup ----

yay -Yc                                   # remove unneeded dependencies
yay -Sc                                   # clean package cache (pacman + yay)
yay -Scc                                  # clean all caches

# clean build directory
rm -rf ~/.cache/yay/                      # remove all build files

# clean specific package build
rm -rf ~/.cache/yay/package/

# check cache size
du -sh ~/.cache/yay/

@code bash
# ---- build directory ----

# default build location
ls ~/.cache/yay/                          # list cached builds

# change build directory
yay --builddir /tmp/yay-builds -S package

@code bash
# ---- PKGBUILD review (diff) ----

# yay shows diffs by default on updates
# control diff behavior:

yay -S package --diffmenu                 # prompt to view diff
yay -S package --nodiffmenu              # skip diff prompt
yay -S package --diff                     # always show diff

# edit PKGBUILD before building
yay -S package --editmenu                 # prompt to edit
yay -S package --noeditmenu              # skip edit prompt

@code bash
# ---- yay configuration ----

# show current config
yay -Y --show

# persistent configuration: ~/.config/yay/config.json
# generated with:
yay --save --cleanafter                   # clean build files after install
yay --save --sudoloop                     # keep sudo alive during builds
yay --save --removemake                   # remove make deps after build
yay --save --provides                     # check AUR for provides
yay --save --batchinstall                 # batch installs for fewer prompts
yay --save --combinedupgrade              # combine repo+AUR upgrade prompts
yay --save --devel                        # check -git packages for updates

@code bash
# ---- yay stats ----

yay -Ps                                   # print system stats
# shows:
#   total installed packages
#   total size
#   top 10 largest packages
#   packages not in a repo (AUR/orphaned)

@code bash
# ---- advanced options ----

# use a specific AUR URL
yay --aururl "https://aur.archlinux.org" -S package

# pass flags to makepkg
yay -S package --mflags "--skippgpcheck"  # skip PGP verification
yay -S package --mflags "--nocheck"       # skip test suite
yay -S package --mflags "-j$(nproc)"      # parallel compilation

# pass flags to git
yay -S package --gitflags "--depth=1"     # shallow clone

# pass flags to pacman
yay -S package --pacmanflags "--overwrite '*'"

@text
Recommended persistent configuration:

@code bash
yay --save --cleanafter --removemake --sudoloop --batchinstall --combinedupgrade

@text
This sets yay to:
- Clean build files after successful install (saves disk)
- Remove make-only dependencies after building
- Keep sudo alive during long compilations
- Batch package installs to reduce prompts
- Combine repo and AUR upgrades into one prompt
